// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded tangent of F64
//
// |x| is reduced to x/(2pi) mod 1 = i/2^11 + X (trig_reduce.tess) and folded into [0, pi/4] by the symmetries
// of the tangent; sin and cos of the reduced argument come out in double-double as for the cosine, and their
// quotient, with an error bound, is tan x or its reciprocal. When the bound can't decide the rounding, the
// accurate path redoes it in 128-bit floating point, dividing through a Newton reciprocal; two arguments that
// path still can't round have their results written out. Round to nearest only: +-0 stay themselves,
// infinities give NaN, a NaN comes back quiet.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/tan/tan.c via RazorForge's B64Tan.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2022-2025 Paul Zimmermann and Tom Hubrecht
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

/// For 0 <= i < 256, TINV[i] = floor(2^127 / (2^63 + i 2^55 + 2^55 - 1)): a 64-bit seed for the inverse of a
/// significand whose top bits after the leading one are i.
